<%# locals: (mcp_url:) %>
<%# How a leader connects Claude to Edify (#323). Shown only to leaders the MCP endpoint serves. It refers to the
    General Handbook only generally (see docs/api.md), and covers Claude's training setting, which the privacy review
    recommended leaders on consumer plans turn off. %>
<div class="card mb-5" id="connect_claude">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h4>Connect Claude</h4>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>
      Claude can answer questions about your unit's speakers, talks, meetings and music from Edify, such as "Who
      hasn't spoken in the last year?"
    </p>

    <h5>Claude on the web, desktop and mobile</h5>
    <ol>
      <li>In Claude on the web or the desktop app, open <strong>Customize &gt; Connectors</strong> and add a custom connector.</li>
      <li>Name it <strong>Edify</strong> and enter this server URL:</li>
    </ol>
    <%= render partial: "settings/connected_apps/copyable", locals: { text: mcp_url } %>
    <ol start="3">
      <li>Select <strong>Connect</strong>, sign in to Edify if asked, and choose <strong>Allow</strong>.</li>
      <li>In a conversation, turn Edify on from the <strong>+</strong> menu. Once connected, it also works in the Claude mobile app.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="text-muted small">
      On a Claude Team or Enterprise plan, an organization owner may need to add the connector first.
    </p>

    <h5>Claude Code</h5>
    <p class="mb-1">Run this in a terminal, then choose Edify under <code>/mcp</code> in Claude Code to sign in:</p>
    <%= render partial: "settings/connected_apps/copyable",
               locals: { text: "claude mcp add --transport http edify #{mcp_url}" } %>

    <h5>What Claude can see</h5>
    <p>
      Only what your role can see in Edify for your unit: members' names, gender and age group (Primary, youth or
      adult), speaking history, meetings and songs. Claude can't change anything, and never sees phone numbers, email
      addresses, notes or birth years.
    </p>

    <h5>Your privacy responsibilities</h5>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Review the Church's guidance on member privacy and the use of AI tools in the
        <%= link_to "General Handbook", ::EdifyConfig.general_handbook_url, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>,
        and use this connection accordingly.
      </li>
      <li>
        On a Claude Free, Pro or Max plan, Anthropic may use your conversations to improve Claude unless you turn off
        <strong>Help improve Claude</strong> under <strong>Settings &gt; Privacy</strong> in Claude.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mb-0">
      To stop Claude's access, disconnect it below. It loses access at once.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
